Ways the change could fail a criterion (what each rating is measured against):

  instability-measurement-prints-usage-table
    [scope_too_narrow] instability-measurement-prints-usage-table/usage-after-finally-uncounted
      The usage footer is printed in the `finally` block before the `InstabilityReport` is built. Any model call made after that point (for example by the comparison client while assembling provenance or the report) is missing from the printed table.
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#3
      pairs: 264 put to the model, 0 skipped once the defect was covered
    [scope_too_narrow] instability-measurement-prints-usage-table/clients-not-all-collected
      Only the comparison client and the clients passed through `run_once` are collected. A client used elsewhere in the measurement (for example by `summarize_model` or `_perturbation_result` via a different client, or a `client_factory` client created outside `run_once`) is left out, and its calls are absent from the table.
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#1
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#2
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#3
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 1 skipped once the defect was covered
    [wrong_output_shape] instability-measurement-prints-usage-table/report-printed-to-stderr-only
      The table is written to stderr via `report`, not to the benchmark's stdout output. If the criterion's "output" means stdout or the benchmark's result output, the table is not in it. The table also prints when the measurement raises, not only when it finishes.
      src/acceptance/usage.py#5
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#3
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 260 skipped once the defect was covered
    [wrong_output_shape] instability-measurement-prints-usage-table/footer-format-diverges
      `render` was changed to append two extra lines (Anthropic credits and other providers) to the footer. This changes the table's shape compared with what `check` and `decompose` print, unless those commands also use this same `render`.
      src/acceptance/usage.py#5
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 260 skipped once the defect was covered
    [other] instability-measurement-prints-usage-table/calls-lost-or-double-counted-by-dedup
      Clients are deduplicated by `id(client)`. Calls are read from `client.observed_calls`. If a client does not accumulate calls in that attribute, as with batched draws or a factory-built client, the table is empty or undercounted.
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#3
      src/acceptance/usage.py#4
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 1 skipped once the defect was covered

  usage-table-covers-every-measurement-call
    [scope_too_narrow] usage-table-covers-every-measurement-call/calls-after-report-omitted
      The usage footer is printed in the `finally` block, before `InstabilityReport` is built. Any model call made while building the report, such as comparison-client calls in the provenance or the final assembly, happens after the footer and is missing from the table.
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#3
      pairs: 264 put to the model, 0 skipped once the defect was covered
    [not_wired] usage-table-covers-every-measurement-call/draw-client-not-registered
      A draw's client is added to `clients` only when the caller passes `clients`. A draw that does not receive the list, such as the perturbed run or a draw reached through another call path, contributes no calls to the table. The append also sits after client construction, so a client that is built but not appended is dropped.
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#1
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#2
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#3
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 1 skipped once the defect was covered
    [other] usage-table-covers-every-measurement-call/identity-dedup-drops-distinct-calls
      Clients are deduplicated by `id()` so that a shared client is counted once. If a factory returns distinct client objects that share one call log, calls are double counted. If it returns one client whose `observed_calls` is replaced or reset per draw, calls from earlier draws are lost. Either way the total differs from the number of calls issued.
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#3
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 1 skipped once the defect was covered
    [missing_case] usage-table-covers-every-measurement-call/summarize-drops-calls-by-stage
      `summarize` groups calls by stage and counts provider calls and replayed calls separately. A call whose stage is missing or unrecognised, or a replayed or batched call, may fall outside the per-stage counts, so the table's per-stage call counts do not sum to N.
      src/acceptance/usage.py#4
      src/acceptance/usage.py#5
      pairs: 12 put to the model, 252 skipped once the defect was covered

  usage-table-live-replayed-counted-apart
    [not_wired] usage-table-live-replayed-counted-apart/report-not-called-on-measurement-path
      The footer is only printed if `report_usage` actually runs on the measurement path. If it were skipped, for example on an early return or an exception path outside the `finally`, no usage table would be printed at the end of the instability measurement.
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#3
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 1 skipped once the defect was covered
    [scope_too_narrow] usage-table-live-replayed-counted-apart/draw-clients-not-collected
      Clients are collected only when `run_once` is given a `clients` list. If a draw's client, such as a perturbed draw's or one built by a `client_factory`, is not appended, its live and replayed calls are missing from the table.
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#1
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#2
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#3
