    [other] usage-table-live-replayed-counted-apart/identity-dedup-miscounts-calls
      Clients are deduplicated by `id()`. Distinct clients are all kept, but a shared client's observed calls could be counted once per draw, or two distinct clients' calls could be collapsed. In either case the live and replayed counts would be inflated or deflated.
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#3
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 1 skipped once the defect was covered
    [other] usage-table-live-replayed-counted-apart/call-counted-in-both-live-and-replayed
      In summarize, the new Anthropic accounting is gated on `from_provider`, and the live/replayed classification is made per call. If a call could be tallied as both live and replayed, or in neither, the two counts would not partition the calls.
