  table-separates-anthropic-spend
    [not_wired] table-separates-anthropic-spend/provider-field-missing-on-calls
      The observed call record's 'provider' key is only set in one place in llm.py and may be absent on other call-record paths (e.g. replayed, embedding, or Jev calls), so summarize's call.get('provider') returns None and Anthropic calls are attributed to 'other providers'.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#2
      src/acceptance/usage.py#4
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 260 skipped once the defect was covered
    [wrong_output_shape] table-separates-anthropic-spend/anthropic-split-only-in-total-lines
      The per-stage table rows do not show the Anthropic-vs-other split; only two summary lines appended after the totals carry it. The 'table' itself may not contain a distinct Anthropic column, and the split is derived only at the footer.
      src/acceptance/usage.py#5
      pairs: 28 put to the model, 236 skipped once the defect was covered
    [other] table-separates-anthropic-spend/other-providers-by-subtraction
      The other-providers figure is computed as total minus Anthropic via float subtraction rather than attributed directly; floating point error can produce tiny negative or inexact values like -0.0000, and it lumps any miscounted call into 'other'.
      src/acceptance/usage.py#5
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 260 skipped once the defect was covered
    [missing_case] table-separates-anthropic-spend/provider-attribution-by-prefix-only
      Attribution relies on provider_of reading the text before the first '/', so a model with no '/' (provider None) or a Claude model served through a different route is silently classified as non-Anthropic; and the 'provider' key is None if model is not a str.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#0
      src/acceptance/llm.py#2
      src/acceptance/config.py#2
      pairs: 124 put to the model, 140 skipped once the defect was covered
    [scope_too_narrow] table-separates-anthropic-spend/instability-footer-misses-calls
      In measure_instability, only clients appended to the list are reported; clients built by other paths (e.g. perturbation, summarize_model internals, batcher) may spend without being included, so the Anthropic spend figure under-counts.
