    [other] provider-routing-by-model-name/provider-label-from-record-model-not-request-model
      The `provider` recorded on an observed call is derived from the `model` taken from the transcript record. This may differ from the configured model the call was actually dispatched with. The provider used for accounting could then disagree with the provider the configured name states.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#2
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 260 skipped once the defect was covered
    [not_wired] provider-routing-by-model-name/batching-and-markers-decided-by-different-tests
      The Anthropic-vs-other decision is made by `is_anthropic_api` for cache markers and batching. Usage accounting uses a separate `call.get('provider') == ANTHROPIC` comparison on a stored label. Calls lacking the `provider` key, such as replayed older records, are counted as non-Anthropic even when the model name states anthropic.
