    [other] provider-decision-single-source/provider-parse-accepts-empty-head
      `provider_of` returns the part before the first `/` whenever a `/` is present, so a name such as '/claude-x' yields an empty-string provider rather than None. The validator accepts it and every consumer treats it as a non-Anthropic provider.
