  spend-excluded-from-review-state-and-report  (reused from an earlier run)
    none enumerated: The diff keeps spend out of review state and the report. `report_usage` calls `print(..., file=sys.stderr)`, so the footer goes to stderr and is never returned or stored. In `measure_instability`, it is called before `InstabilityReport` is built, and its result (None) is not passed in. The new `provider` key is added only to the in-memory observed-call dicts, and `clients` holds only client objects. The new `anthropic_*` fields live on `StageUsage` and `RunUsage`, which are usage models, not review state or report models. `render` is the footer renderer, not the report renderer. Nothing in the diff writes spend into `Review`, `RunSnapshot`, `InstabilityReport` or the provenance, so no static path violates the invariant.

