  anthropic-credits-own-figure/provider-from-model-name-prefix-only
    Lines 257-258 of provider_of take the text before the first '/' as the provider and return None for any name without '/'. is_anthropic_api (line 267) and the Anthropic-credit sums in usage.py (line 240) therefore match only names that start with 'anthropic/'. A bare Claude name such as 'claude-3-5-sonnet' is billed to Anthropic's own API but is recorded with provider None, so it falls into 'other providers'. That is the DEFECTIVE behaviour. The repair makes a bare 'claude…' name resolve to ANTHROPIC. It contradicts the docstring's statement that a name with no '/' states no provider, so this reading of 'expected' is a judgement. I did not handle non-'anthropic' prefixes that route to Anthropic, since the code gives no way to tell which prefixes those are.
